  "id": "participant-observation",
  "term": "participant observation",
  "definition": "Participant observation is a research method used in ethnographic work in which the researcher observes people’s activities by being present within their real-life settings and events. In this packet, it involves closely watching practices and interactions across rehearsals, teaching, festivals, and performances to build a detailed understanding of lived behavior in context.",
